      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>ca</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>ca is an optional reference to a config map by name containing the PEM-encoded CA bundle. It is used as a trust anchor to validate the TLS certificate presented by the remote server. The key "ca.crt" is used to locate the data. If specified and the config map or expected key is not found, the identity provider is not honored. If the specified ca data is not valid, the identity provider is not honored. If empty, the default system roots are used. This can only be configured when hostname is set to a non-empty value. The namespace for this config map is openshift-config.</TableCell>
